    "directions": [
      "In a sauce pot, add gooseberries, mango ginger, sugar, water, ginger, fennel seeds, jaggery, cover it with the lid and cook for 12-15 minutes or until everything is cooked. Transfer it into the bowl and leave it aside to cool down the temperature.",
      "Transfer it into the mixer grinder jar and grind it into a smooth fine paste. keep it aside for further use.",
      "In a sauce pan, add water, ragi flour and cook it on low flames for a while until it is properly cooked. Transfer it into the bowl and keep it aside for further use.",
      "In a saucepot or handi, add kolam rice, water, cover it with the lid and cook for 20-25 minutes until rice gets mushy in texture. Transfer it to a bowl and leave it aside for further use.",
      "In a serving bowl, add onion, green chillies, fresh coriander leaves, cooked ragi mixture and give it a good mix. Add ice cubes, curd, water, salt to taste, lemon juice and give it a good mix. Transfer it into the serving glass and serve chilled.",
      "In a mortar pestle, add lemon leaves, mango ginger, green chilli and grind it into a coarse paste. Keep it aside for further use.",
      "In a clay pot, add cooked rice, sufficient water and cover it with a muslin cloth and keep it aside for fermentation for 1 day or at least 18-20 hours.",
      "In a clay pot, add fermented rice water, curd, prepared torani paste, curry leaves, fresh red chilli, lemon, lemon juice, salt to taste, cumin powder and give it a good mix. Transfer it into the serving glass or clay glass and serve chilled.",
      "In a serving bowl or jar, add grated gooseberry, ginger, crushed black peppercorns. Add prepared amla paste, ice cubes, water as required, a pinch of salt, fresh mint leaves and mix everything well. Transfer it into the serving glass, garnish it with lemon slices, mint sprig and ice cubes. Serve chilled."
    ],
